cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "diorthosis: compiling published critical editions into TEI and AI-ready Markdown"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Girardi
    given-names: Romain
    affiliation: "CEPAM UMR 7264, Université Côte d'Azur"
repository-code: "https://github.com/romain-girardi-eng/diorthosis"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - critical-edition
  - apparatus-criticus
  - TEI
  - digital-humanities
  - classics
  - textual-criticism
abstract: >-
  diorthosis compiles published critical editions (born-digital PDFs, or the
  ALTO/hOCR output of any OCR engine) into TEI P5 with the apparatus criticus
  split, anchored to its in-text markers and preserved verbatim, plus a
  deterministic AI-ready Markdown view (md-ce) rendered from the same model.
  Block-level provenance distinguishes decoded from OCR-generated text
  permanently.
